{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <stddef.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f\\n\\nstatic double *grid;\\nstatic double *new_grid;\\nstatic int size;\\nstatic int iter_max_num;\\n\\nstatic inline double absolute(double num) {\\n    return num < 0.0 ? -num : num;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void allocate_memory(void) {\\n    const size_t cells = (size_t)size * (size_t)size;\\n    grid = (double *)malloc(cells * sizeof(*grid));\\n    new_grid = (double *)malloc(cells * sizeof(*new_grid));\\n}\\n\\nstatic void initialize_grid(void) {\\n    const int center = size / 2;\\n    const int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    const int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\\n        const size_t row = (size_t)i * (size_t)size;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; ++j) {\\n            const double value = (i >= linf && i <= lsup &&\\n                                  j >= linf && j <= lsup) ? 100.0 : 0.0;\\n            grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\\n            new_grid[row + (size_t)j] =\\n                (i == 0 || i == size - 1 || j == 0 || j == size - 1) ? value : 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic void save_grid(void) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\\n        const size_t row = (size_t)i * (size_t)size;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; ++j) {\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[row + (size_t)j]);\\n        }\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\\n    (void)argc;\\n    (void)argv;\\n\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n\\n    allocate_memory();\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    int has_error = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n    int stop = 0;\\n    int iteration_error = 0;\\n\\n    /* Keep one team alive across iterations while alternating contiguous buffers. */\\n    #pragma omp parallel shared(has_error, iter, stop, iteration_error, grid, new_grid)\\n    {\\n        while (1) {\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            {\\n                stop = !(has_error && iter < iter_max_num);\\n                if (!stop) {\\n                    iteration_error = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            if (stop) {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n\\n            double *restrict current = grid;\\n            double *restrict next = new_grid;\\n\\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(| : iteration_error)\\n            for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; ++i) {\\n                const size_t row_offset = (size_t)i * (size_t)size;\\n                const double *restrict row = current + row_offset;\\n                const double *restrict above = row - size;\\n                const double *restrict below = row + size;\\n                double *restrict output = next + row_offset;\\n                int row_error = 0;\\n\\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(| : row_error)\\n                for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; ++j) {\\n                    const double value = 0.25 * (row[j + 1] + row[j - 1] +\\n                                                 above[j] + below[j]);\\n                    output[j] = value;\\n                    row_error |= absolute(value - row[j]) > CONV_THRESHOLD;\\n                }\\n                iteration_error |= row_error;\\n            }\\n\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            {\\n                double *temporary = grid;\\n                grid = new_grid;\\n                new_grid = temporary;\\n                has_error = iteration_error;\\n                ++iter;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    save_grid();\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"A contiguous row-major ping-pong layout removes the copy sweep, and retaining one OpenMP team across all iterations avoids repeated fork/join overhead while static row ownership and SIMD-friendly contiguous inner loops improve locality on four ARM64 cores.\",\"notes\":\"Both alternating buffers preserve the fixed boundary values, including degenerate valid grid sizes; each stencil expression, strict convergence comparison, stopping condition, and output format are retained.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Replace per-row allocations with two contiguous row-major buffers.\",\"Use buffer swapping instead of the interior copy sweep while preserving boundary values in both buffers.\",\"Use a persistent OpenMP parallel region with static row work-sharing, boolean OR reduction, and SIMD inner-loop annotation.\"]}"}}
